Wait! I remember this code!
"Any invalid calls for templateUrls are under app/* and should return 404"
"Any deep link calls should return index.html"
If this is the code in 0.0.12, then they ADDED the `/app/*` 404 handler!
Let's check the snippet provided in the prompt.
```javascript
switch (environment){
    case 'build':
        console.log('** BUILD **');
        app.use(express.static('./build/'));
        app.use('/*', express.static('./build/index.html'));
        break;
    default:
        console.log('** DEV **');
        app.use(express.static('./src/client/'));
        app.use(express.static('./'));
        app.use('/*', express.static('./src/client/index.html'));
        break;
}
```
Yes! The snippet in the prompt DOES NOT have the `/app/*` 404 handler!
So the fix was to add the `/app/*` 404 handler!
Wait, if they added the `/app/*` 404 handler, how does it fix the XSS?
If a user requests `/app/<script>alert(1)</script>`, it matches `/app/*`, and the new 404 handler catches it and returns a safe 404 response, preventing it from falling through to the default Express 404 handler!
