If they request `/foo/...`, it matches `/*`, which uses `express.static('./build/index.html')`.
Wait, if `express.static` calls `next()`, it falls through to the default Express 404 handler!
So adding `/app/*` only fixes XSS for URLs starting with `/app/`!
