Yes, this is exactly $O(N \times U)$, where $N$ is the length of the string and $U$ is the number of unique characters $\ge$ the initial `n`.
If all characters are unique, $U \approx N$, so it's $O(N^2)$.
So `_punycode` is DEFINITELY $O(N^2)$.
Therefore, the ONLY way to fix the DoS in `encode()` is to restrict the length of the label BEFORE calling `_punycode`.
Since `check_label` is called right before `_punycode`, restricting the length before `check_label` fixes BOTH vulnerabilities!

